# Worklist stewardship

`docs/platform/WORKLIST.md` is the **only** active platform worklist. Design
notes, ops runbooks, review ledgers, and `docs/NEEDS-OPERATOR.md` are evidence
sources — never present a second file as an active tracker.

## Epic shape

Heading: `### WL-<FAMILY>-<NNN> - <title>` (space-hyphen-space). Required
fields, in this order:

Status, Priority, Complexity, Problem, Required outcome, Current state,
Remaining work, Scope, Relevant files/components, Acceptance criteria,
Verification method, Origin or merged source IDs.

Optional: `Dependencies`. No `Progress` field. No checkbox markers.

Status is exactly `Remaining` / `Blocked` / `Needs clarification`. Do not
leave a completed epic in the active file.

## Parallel drain unit (required for Remaining)

`AI_GOVERNANCE.md` §10.0.4 makes the DRAIN-ENGINE the canonical parallel
surface. Every `Status: Remaining` epic MUST carry at least one
`@farm:{cargo …}` payload — the canonical carrier is the `Verification
method:` field, appended inline:

```
- Verification method: focused mde-collab-egui farm gate. @farm:{cargo test -p mde-collab-egui}
```

Multiple markers on one epic authorise disjoint parallel workers. A
non-`cargo …` payload (e.g. `@farm:{crate,verify}`) is a template and
contributes zero demand — do not stuff prose inside the braces.

The queue this feeds is `automation/lib/farm-jobs.sh active` →
`automation/queue/farm-enqueue.sh` → the etcd `/farm/queue/*` consumed by
`automation/queue/farm-agent.sh`. Tick with
`install-helpers/drain-coordinator.sh plan`. Do not invent a second queue.

After commit/push, fill with `automation/reconciler/tick-fill.sh` (or
`systemctl start --no-block mcnf-farm-reconcile.service`). The path unit
`mcnf-farm-reconcile.path` starts the same oneshot on HEAD change; do
not wait for the 15-min timer, and do not hand-fan a command the
reconciler already owns.

`Status: Blocked` and `Status: Needs clarification` epics may omit the
payload but should record what would unblock the payload landing.

## Close and evidence

- Done or retired items move to `docs/worklist-archive/` with a disposition
  (done + evidence path, or retired + reason + successor). Never reuse an ID.
- A story is incomplete until deliverable, hostile/regression test, farm
  command and result, and required live/package evidence are in
  `docs/platform/evidence/`. A passing compile is not completion.
- Missing hardware, provider access, credentials, or capacity fails the owning
  automated gate. It is never a passing substitute or an operator handoff.
- Fixtures must not satisfy production gates (`AI_GOVERNANCE.md` §7).

## Hygiene

Update the snapshot Remaining/Blocked/Needs-clarification counts so they match
parsed epics. Keep lines and epic bodies inside `lint-worklist.sh` limits.

Before landing worklist edits:

```bash
install-helpers/lint-worklist.sh --self-test
install-helpers/lint-worklist.sh
```
